cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, simulation architecture, or kinematic mapping methodology in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ROS 2 MediaPipe Robotic Hand: Real-Time Teleoperation Digital Twin"
abstract: >-
  A fully containerized, vision-based digital twin of a 15-DOF robotic hand. A standard RGB webcam
  feeds Google MediaPipe Hands, whose 21 spatial landmarks are converted into 15 anatomical joint
  angles by vector dot product, normalized into a flexion ratio, and linearly interpolated onto the
  mechanical joint limits of a CAD-exported URDF. The resulting joint states drive a digital twin in
  ROS 2 Jazzy and RViz in real time. The stack runs as a set of Docker Compose services with X11
  forwarding, GPU and webcam passthrough, and includes the full CAD-to-URDF export pipeline from
  Onshape.
